                                                "sense_id": "071b5c2e-d9ba-3709-94a0-a32f24d71379",
                                                "text": "I did this in thirty pages of closely written matter, of which a pressed copy remains in my commonplace-book."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c295662-fb79-4bfd-801a-858b757c7315",
                                                "sense_id": "071b5c2e-d9ba-3709-94a0-a32f24d71379",
                                                "text": "The compiler of a commonplace book is on his own; he can put in anything that appeals to him: aphorisms, poems, parts of poems, newspaper clippings, song lyrics, bits of humor, overheard conversations—anything that has struck him as exciting, that he has found stimulating, odd or amusing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f278b630-c804-4def-be1d-f335a8b0508c",
                                                "sense_id": "071b5c2e-d9ba-3709-94a0-a32f24d71379",
                                                "text": "But the other kind of commonplace book was different. Its goal was to gather a collection of the wisest statements, usually of the ancients, for future meditation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8043980-47cd-44a5-841a-83355fc6425d",
                                                "sense_id": "071b5c2e-d9ba-3709-94a0-a32f24d71379",
                                                "text": "Popularized in a previous period of information overload, the Industrial Revolution of the eighteenth and early nineteenth centuries, the commonplace book was more than a diary or journal of personal reflections. It was a learning tool that the educated class used to understand a rapidly changing world and their place in it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cf497e95-449b-4bfa-beee-63deebc4a3c2",
                        "source_entry_id": "7509a51f-348a-3e62-81f4-1a5b95562d53",
                        "source_sense_id": "2c9d712a-4b0f-33f1-9bac-e67fe4f920ff",
                        "source_sense_description": "Buch oder Heft, in dem man Notizen, Gedanken, Ideen, Skizzen oder Aphorismen sammelt; Kollektaneenbuch",
                        "target_lang_word": "notebook",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "notebook",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3b774c05-3dfe-3434-9c89-9f56c1972e83",
                                        "entry_id": "6956d866-b77a-34cd-b41a-96184181c4fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A book in which notes or memoranda are written."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f661450-213c-41fc-a3b8-9206f8e320a5",
                                                "sense_id": "3b774c05-3dfe-3434-9c89-9f56c1972e83",
                                                "text": "With an unquenchable enthusiasm for locomotives and their work, at an early age I had commenced to keep engine and traffic-recording notebooks, compiled in a schoolboy's round hand."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0157a3e9-dd49-4ada-8d39-fe4dc6d334b8",
                                                "sense_id": "3b774c05-3dfe-3434-9c89-9f56c1972e83",
                                                "text": "For Caſſius is a-weary of the World: / Hated by one he loues, brau'd by his Brother, / Check'd like a bondman, all his faults obſeru'd, / Set in a Note-booke, learn'd, and con'd by roate / To caſt into my Teeth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf7f7f95-836f-3b9d-8f39-47f35b6926ec",
                                        "entry_id": "6956d866-b77a-34cd-b41a-96184181c4fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A kind of user interface in literate programming, allowing calculations to be interspersed with human-readable comments, diagrams, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "attributive",
                                            "sometimes"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dfd2549f-63de-4550-a6fc-2f2b9a683248",
                                                "sense_id": "cf7f7f95-836f-3b9d-8f39-47f35b6926ec",
                                                "text": "We have found the use of Jupyter notebooks to be a convenient way of sharing work and code in a compact and reproducible manner. Jupyter notebooks are easy to update and adapt over time compared to a static CD-ROM."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "898cce50-6c35-3728-82a1-b1dc45f9598d",
                                        "entry_id": "6956d866-b77a-34cd-b41a-96184181c4fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of notebook computer (“laptop computer”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "599f9bba-fd5d-4e01-9848-9aeb3a34ff61",
                                                "sense_id": "898cce50-6c35-3728-82a1-b1dc45f9598d",
                                                "text": "Over time, the difference in size between laptops and notebooks became a matter of no more than an inch or two in length and width, and a fraction of an inch in thickness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
